// =======================================================================================
// The strings of the interface -- one file per language, res/lang/<tag>.rc.
// =======================================================================================
//
// Stage L10N, task T-L10N-2 (decisions 198.14, 198.16): until then the fourteen languages stood
// here, two string tables each. They moved out unchanged, and the built RT_STRING resource is
// byte for byte what it was (gate 5 of the stage). Each file declares the UTF-8 code page itself
// and sets its own LANGUAGE; the order of the #include lines is the order of the language combo
// box, `Language::ALL`. The registry of the languages is res/lang/languages.toml, the context of
// every string res/lang/context.tsv, the guard of the files tests/l10n.rs.
//
// ⚠ Nothing may follow the last #include: the LANGUAGE it sets stays in force to the end of the
// script, and a resource added below it would take the language of Arabic.
//
// The rules below were written above the tables they govern, and govern every file of res/lang.
//
// ⚠ A backslash is an escape character in an .rc string. `HKCU\…\Run` has to be written
// `HKCU\\…\\Run`, and a `"` inside a string has to be doubled. Neither mistake is loud.
//
// `{0}`, `{1}`, `{2}` are filled in by `settings::format_text`; the substitution is textual
// and takes numbers and names the program itself produced — never a keystroke (SEC-01).
//
// ⚠ **«Lang Switcher» is not translated** and reads the same in both locales — decision on
// question 7. It is the display name of the product: the caption below, the value name under
// `HKCU\…\Run` (`settings::AUTOSTART_VALUE_NAME`) and the about box all carry it unchanged.
//
// The two entries of the language combo box are **not** in either table on purpose: a
// language is named in its own language in a language chooser, so «Русский» and «English»
// stand as they are whichever locale is in force.

// =======================================================================================
// The ten locales of tier one — решение 93, task Т-28-3.
// =======================================================================================
//
// ⚠ **The code page governs these ten exactly as it governs the two above**, and here it is
// load-bearing in ten alphabets at once: Cyrillic, Greek, the carons of Czech, the ogoneks of
// Polish, the dotless ı of Turkish. `#pragma code_page(65001)` above the tables is what makes
// them survive `rc.exe`, and the damage it prevents is silent — mojibake builds green and
// tests green until somebody looks at the window. The instrument that watches for it is
// `scratchpad-Э28\мохибейк-греп.ps1`, and it is run after every one of these blocks.
//
// ⚠ Every string here obeys `scratchpad-Э28\глоссарий.md`: one agreed word per term per
// language, decided **before** the first translation was written. A translation that reads
// well but names a term differently from the glossary is a defect of the translation.
//
// ⚠ «Lang Switcher» is not translated in any of the twelve — the decision on question 7.
// Neither are the key names (`Esc`, `Ctrl`, `Alt`, `Shift`, `F12`, `Pause`) or `%APPDATA%`.
// `{0}`, `{1}`, `{2}` keep their number and their count; only their place may move.
//
// The order below is the order of the language combo box, which is `Language::ALL`.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Hebrew and Arabic, the two right-to-left locales of вопрос 97. Task Т-30-1.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The tables themselves carry **no direction marks** — no U+200E, no U+200F, no isolates.
// Direction is decided by the code: the window is mirrored by the extended style its template
// is created with (task Т-30-2) and an island of Latin text is turned back to left-to-right
// reading by one function (task Т-30-4). A mark buried in a translation would make an island
// silently, and no sweep over these tables would ever see it — the string would look ordinary.
// The sweep `no_translation_carries_a_direction_mark` in `tests\settings.rs` is the guard.
//
// The arrow of IDS_ABOUT_HELP_5 is «←» and not «→»: it leads the eye from the first place
// named to the second, and in a right-to-left line the first of them stands on the right.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The same menu in the ten locales of tier one — решение 93, task Т-28-3.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// ⚠ «Запускать при входе в систему» is the **same sentence** as `IDS_AUTOSTART` of the dialog
// above, and it is translated the same way in every locale on purpose: one action, one wording,
// two places it can be reached from. A test compares the two rows in all twelve tables.

